    "created_at": "2021-11-23T15:24:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-23T15:24:06Z",
    "body": "We've been discussing https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/issues/229 and I think we might need a separate list of source ports to block for UDP-based protocols.\r\n\r\nFrom the point of view of a NAT device, a TCP connection has a clear client and server, so usually only the destination port is interesting. But UDP is more ambiguous, and a packet going from an internet host to a client may cause a NAT binding to be formed.\r\n\r\nRegardless, the WebTransport W3C standard would like to delegate to the Fetch standard for the list of ports to block.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
